WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Type sine of one hundred and
fifty degrees into your GDC.

2
00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.540
It says one half.

3
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.110
Now try sine of thirty degrees.

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.240
One half again.

5
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.320
Exactly.

6
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.310
Two very different angles, one answer.

7
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.350
A rounding fluke, or something deeper?

8
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.980
In this mission, you'll turn a radius
anticlockwise around a circle of radius

9
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:21.900
one.

10
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.030
Its end point is cos theta, sin theta.

11
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.110
So sine is just the height of that point.

12
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.470
You'll also see that the quadrant
decides the signs of sine and cosine.

13
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.740
So why should two angles
so far apart share a sine?

14
00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:41.770
Your mission: explain why sine of one
hundred and fifty degrees is exactly equal

15
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.550
to sine of thirty degrees.
